# Question: on a daemon where every configured user's login-service set is empty
# (excluding every door) and command authorization denies everything by default,
# does the stored ZeFS recovery user still authenticate and execute commands on
# SSH, ze cli, Web (Basic + form), REST, and gRPC while the config account is
# refused everywhere?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: only seeding a real ZeFS store with `ze init`
# and booting a live daemon proves usersFromStore -> mergeAuthUsers ->
# ReservedRecoveryProfile exempts the recovery identity across all four live listeners.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-8 (OD-2 option a) -- unshadowed stored recovery user survives full lockout
# PREVENTS: login-service restrictions locking out the break-glass stored recovery user

option=timeout:value=60s
option=storage:value=disk
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/login-service-recovery-user $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=50s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: ordinary config account refused on SSH, Web, REST, and gRPC
expect=stderr:contains=OK: stored recovery user authenticated on SSH, ze cli, Web, REST, and gRPC
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
